CellCharterR installation (Linux CPU)
====================================

The supported validation target for this release is x86_64 Linux on CPU. The
compiled C++ backend and all SPE import/downstream APIs do not require R Torch
or LibTorch. In particular, loading a legacy disk-backed SPE never initializes
Torch or downloads a runtime.

1. Install the current Bioconductor release/development dependencies.
2. Install CellCharterR and run the tiny compiled-CPU smoke test or beginner
   vignette.

The experimental Torch backend is optional. Only if it is explicitly needed,
install `torch` from CRAN and its CPU runtime, then verify it:

       Rscript -e 'install.packages("torch")'
       Rscript -e 'torch::install_torch(type = "cpu")'
       Rscript -e 'library(torch); print(torch::torch_randn(2, 2, device = "cpu"))'

Package builds, checks, examples, and vignettes do not download LibTorch,
H5AD files, or the full mouse-spleen dataset. Full-data downloads shown in the
conversion vignette are opt-in and unevaluated.

Windows, macOS, Linux ARM, CUDA, and full-dataset platform validation are not
claimed for this release.
